### GATEWAY  ·  http://localhost:3000
###
### Everything above is proxied. These two routes are the gateway's own.
###
### GET /books/:id/page composes a book with its reviews at read time, and the
### two dependencies are NOT symmetric:
###   book-service    REQUIRED  — no book, no page
###   review-service  OPTIONAL  — the page renders without it, reviews marked
###                               "unavailable" (which is not the same as none)
###
### Fixtures: run books.http and reviews.http first, or reuse a known id.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@email = amr@example.com
@password = password123


### Health  →  200
GET {{baseUrl}}/health


### Log in + a book with a review, so the page has something to compose
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

@accessToken = {{login.response.body.data.tokens.accessToken}}

###
# @name pageBook
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{ "title": "Composed Page Fixture", "description": "Has at least one review.", "genre": ["test"] }

@bookId = {{pageBook.response.body.data.id}}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookId": "{{bookId}}", "rating": 5, "comment": "Composed." }


### The composed page  →  200, book + reviews in one response
### reviews carries items + hasMore + total. The gateway asks review-service for
### a fixed number (REVIEWS_ON_PAGE), so one page view can no longer cost
### whatever the most-reviewed book happens to hold.
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/{{bookId}}/page


### Degraded: stop review-service, then resend the request above.
### Expect 200 with reviews marked unavailable — NOT an empty array, which
### would assert "this book has no reviews".
###   docker stop review-service   →  resend  →  docker start review-service


### Missing book  →  404, because book-service is the required half
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/page
